cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the RobustBench benchmark, please cite the paper."
title: "Variant-aware CDR-H3 design improves predicted binding across antigen variation"
abstract: >-
  Antibody sequence generators normally condition on a single fixed antigen structure.
  This work steers a frozen generator at inference time with a CVaR-aggregated
  binding objective evaluated across multiple plausible antigen variants, and evaluates
  the resulting CDR-H3 designs on held-out antigen variants never seen during design.
  Includes RobustBench, a 200-complex antibody escape-robustness benchmark.
